<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nioro du Sahel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nioro du <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a> is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayes">Kayes</a> Region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, close to the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a>. It became the capital of the Bambara kingdom of Kaarta, was taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toucouleur">Toucouleur</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall">El Hadj Umar Tall</a> in 1854 and served as a stronghold of his empire until the French captured it in 1891.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nioro-du-sahel.jpg" alt="Nioro du Sahel" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gregor Rom · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nioro.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
